Part III — The Four Components

9. GCIL-T: Transport

9.1 Typed Structure

Definition 9.1 (Transport). T is a tuple (P_{\mathrm{transport}}, \mathrm{Discovery}, \mathrm{Binding}, \mathrm{Version}) where P_{\mathrm{transport}} is a set of protocols (A2A, UACP), \mathrm{Discovery} a relation on AgentCards, \mathrm{Binding} a transport binding function, and \mathrm{Version} a version negotiation relation.

9.2 Adoption

GCIL-T adopts A2A v1.0 as primary and UACP as alternative. GCIL is specified as an A2A extension: the Epistemic Bundle is carried as a typed artifact, and the GCIL version is advertised in the AgentCard.

Proposition 9.1 (No transport innovation). GCIL-T introduces no new transport primitive.

Proof. By construction of Definition 9.1: every component of T is an existing transport protocol. ∎

10. GCIL-K: Knowledge Reconciliation

10.1 Adoption

GCIL-K adopts MELD's five-outcome procedure (insert, merge, relate, conflict, reject) over three signals: scoped claim-key identity, embedding similarity, NLI verdict.

10.2 Conflict vs. Truth

\boxed{
\mathrm{Conflict\ detection} \neq \mathrm{truth\ adjudication}
}

Proposition 10.1. GCIL-K preserves detected contradictions.

Proof. By construction: the admission procedure outputs conflict for candidates that fail the merge criterion, and the status CRDT records this state without resolution. No further Act is applied by the admission procedure itself. ∎

10.3 False-Merge Hazard

Definition 10.2 (False Merge). A false merge is an admission outcome of merge on candidates that should remain distinct.

Proposition 10.2. A false merge is a silent mutation in the sense of NSM-2 if and only if the merged claim is not recoverable from the journal.

Proof. If the merge Act records both input claims and the merge criterion, then the merge is recoverable. If it records only the output, the merge is silent. The journal structure of §3.4 records inputs and outputs by construction, so false merges are recoverable but not prevented. ∎

10.4 Related Work

The prior art of eSPARQL (four-valued logic over RDF-star), nanopublications (three-graph structure: assertion, provenance, publication info), and W3C PROV establishes that atomic, provenance-carrying claims are a mature concept. GCIL's contribution is the governed integration of such claims under enforceable invariants, not the atomic claim primitive itself.

11. GCIL-P: Provenance

11.1 Adoption

EWS for cryptographic header schema, ETICS for compliance layer mapping, TRACE for runtime attestation.

11.2 Verifiable ≠ True

\boxed{
\mathrm{Verifiable(Provenance)} \neq \mathrm{True(Provenance)}
}

Proposition 11.1. Cryptography establishes identity, integrity, signature, and timestamp. It does not establish intellectual independence of sources.

Proof. A signature establishes that a producer signed a message. It does not establish that the producer's evidence is not derived from another producer's evidence. Independence is a property of the derivation DAG, not of the signature. ∎

11.3 TRACE Category

TRACE attests where and how something ran. It does not attest that a claim is sound. This is a category-adjacent contribution, integrated as an optional runtime attestation, not a provenance guarantee.

12. GCIL-S: Sovereignty

12.1 Principle

\boxed{
\mathrm{Disclosure} \subseteq \mathrm{AuthorizedMinimum(Request, Policy)}
}

This is stricter than \mathrm{Data}_{\mathrm{private}} \notin \mathrm{Network}: it bounds what is disclosed, not merely whether raw data is transmitted.

12.2 Layer-Specific Privacy Defenses

DP-Flames defends federated training of KG embeddings against membership inference. It does not cover disclosure leaks during bundle exchange (existence, size, timing, confidence).

Definition 12.1 (Per-Request Defense). For each request R and policy \Pi, define

\mathrm{Disclose}(R, \Pi) = \mu_{\Pi}(R) \subseteq \mathrm{Content}(R)

where \mu_{\Pi} is a policy-parameterized minimization function.

Proposition 12.1. For any non-trivial \Pi, \mathrm{Disclose}(R, \Pi) is strictly contained in \mathrm{Content}(R).

Proof. By definition of \mu_{\Pi} as a minimization function with a non-empty policy constraint set. ∎

12.3 Composed Sybil Defense

Definition 12.2 (Reputation).

\mathrm{Rep}(i) = \mathrm{LinkAnalysis}(i) \times \mathrm{FlowGate}(i)

Proposition 12.2. Neither factor alone suffices.

Proof. Link analysis does not resist Sybil attacks on its own (a Sybil cluster can be internally well-connected); flow-based gating does not produce a reputation ordering within the honest region (it only bounds flow). Composition is necessary. ∎

