Appendix D — Policy Acts: Complete Specification with Proofs

D.1 PolicyChange

Definition D.1. A PolicyChange Act is:

A_{\mathrm{PC}} = (p, \tau, \texttt{PolicyChange}, \iota, o, \sigma, \kappa, \mathsf{pol})

where \iota = \{h(\Pi_{\mathrm{base}}), \mathrm{target}\}, o = \{h(\rho)\}, and \rho = (\delta, \mathrm{base}, \mathrm{target}, \mathrm{proposer}).

Preconditions.

1. h(\Pi_{\mathrm{base}}) = h(\Pi_{t-1}) (fresh base).
2. \mathrm{target} \in \{\pi_{vis}, \pi_{adm}, \pi_{gov}\}.
3. \delta does not touch I_{\mathrm{core}}.

Postconditions. \rho is recorded in the pending proposal set \mathcal{R}.

D.2 PolicyEndorse

Definition D.2. A PolicyEndorse Act is:

A_{\mathrm{PE}} = (p, \tau, \texttt{PolicyEndorse}, \{h(\rho)\}, \varnothing, \sigma, \kappa, \mathsf{pol})

Preconditions. \rho \in \mathcal{R}.

Postconditions. p's endorsement is added to \rho.\mathrm{endorsers}.

D.3 PolicyEnact

Definition D.3. A PolicyEnact Act is:

A_{\mathrm{PEn}} = (p, \tau, \texttt{PolicyEnact}, \{h(\rho)\}, \{h(\Pi')\}, \sigma, \kappa, \mathsf{pol})

where \Pi' = \mathrm{Apply}(\Pi_{t-1}, \rho.\delta).

Preconditions (E1–E4).

· E1 (Quorum). |\{e \in \rho.\mathrm{endorsers} : \forall e' \neq e, \mathrm{Ind}(e, e') \land I_e < p_{\max}\}| \geq k_{\mathrm{target}}.
· E2 (Contestation). \tau \geq \rho.\tau + \tau_{\mathrm{win}} and every Challenge against \rho is adjudicated.
· E3 (Fresh base). \rho.\mathrm{base} = h(\Pi_{t-1}).
· E4 (Core immunity). \rho.\delta \cap I_{\mathrm{core}} = \varnothing.

Postconditions. \Pi_t = \Pi', v' = v + 1, h_{\mathrm{parent}} = h(\Pi_{t-1}).

D.4 Proposition D.1 (Enactment Determinism)

Proposition. \Pi' = \mathrm{Apply}(\Pi, \delta) is a function.

Proof. \mathrm{Apply} is defined as componentwise update:

\mathrm{Apply}(\Pi, \delta) = \Pi[\mathrm{target} \mapsto \delta(\Pi.\mathrm{target}), v \mapsto v+1, h_{\mathrm{parent}} \mapsto h(\Pi)]

This is a deterministic operation on the tuple. ∎

D.5 Proposition D.2 (No Self-Ratification)

Proposition. \mathrm{Valid}(A_{\mathrm{PEn}}) = \top iff all preconditions E1–E4 hold under \Pi_{t-1}, never under \Pi'.

Proof. By Definition D.3, the preconditions are evaluated against \Pi_{t-1} because \rho.\mathrm{base} = h(\Pi_{t-1}) and \rho.\tau + \tau_{\mathrm{win}} \leq \tau. The output \Pi' is not used in the precondition evaluation. ∎

D.6 Proposition D.3 (Non-Retroactivity)

Proposition. A PolicyEnact at index j affects validity only for indices > j.

Proof. By Definition D.3, the output \Pi' is stored at position j. For i \leq j, \mathrm{Valid}(A_i) is evaluated against \Pi_{i-1}. Since \Pi_{i-1} is unchanged by the enactment at j (it was determined before j), the validity of A_i is unchanged. ∎

D.7 Proposition D.4 (Core Amendment Rejection)

Proposition. Any PolicyChange with \delta \cap I_{\mathrm{core}} \neq \varnothing is rejected at construction.

Proof. By precondition E4 of Definition D.3. ∎

